\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (a) Real secondary-valve events versus model probes: the plant's response builds over minutes and ends negative on most windows; the physics line's 60-step terminal response sign-inverted before the repair batch and is sign-consistent after it; the deep forecaster stays inside $\pm $0.04~\si {\degreeCelsius }. (b) One-step error by channel: the physics line is near persistence at the terminal stage and 38$\times $ worse upstream. (c) Residual means by load quintile: the terminal-stage bias is flat after retraining, the upstream stage swings 5--13~\si {\degreeCelsius }.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:evidence}{{3}{7}{(a) Real secondary-valve events versus model probes: the plant's response builds over minutes and ends negative on most windows; the physics line's 60-step terminal response sign-inverted before the repair batch and is sign-consistent after it; the deep forecaster stays inside $\pm $0.04~\si {\degreeCelsius }. (b) One-step error by channel: the physics line is near persistence at the terminal stage and 38$\times $ worse upstream. (c) Residual means by load quintile: the terminal-stage bias is flat after retraining, the upstream stage swings 5--13~\si {\degreeCelsius }}{figure.3}{}}
